{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
REVYTECH Wayfire stack — post-install privilege validation

On install, revytech-desktop-privileges-enable VALIDATE-then-APPLYs:

  * group video     — seatd / DRM (display modeset, compositor)
  * group operator  — setuid /sbin/shutdown (power off/reboot without doas)
  * seatd_enable    — and start seatd if needed
  * narrow doas rules for ifconfig / wpa_cli / zzz (network + suspend)
  * system defaults (dpms never, panel top) when package files are present

Re-run anytime:
  doas revytech-desktop-privileges-enable
  doas revytech-desktop-privileges-enable --check   # validate only

After group membership changes, log out and log back in (or reboot) so the
Wayfire session picks up operator/video in getgroups().

Session launch: /usr/local/libexec/wayfire-session-launch
Config hierarchy: ~/.config/wayfire.ini → /usr/local/etc/wayfire/wayfire.ini
Docs: /usr/local/share/doc may not include DESKTOP-PRIVILEGES.md; see
  https://github.com/revytechinc/wf-shell/blob/master/docs/DESKTOP-PRIVILEGES.md
EOM
}
